{
  "version": 2,
  "name": "Ashford Police Station",
  "kind": "Complex",
  "description": "Police station with 2 floors. On the first floor there is the lobby/reception area, 2 toilets, break room, storage room and the carage. On the second floor there are 4 cells and 3 office rooms. Fill the space up so there is no leftover space. There should also be the \u0022main\u0022 entrance on the south side, along with the carage entrance. One the west side there should be a side entrance. There should be a backdoor leading to the alleyway, it should be in either a hallway connecting the different rooms or the break room. It should not be from the storage or toilets. The whole building is on a slightly elevated base, there should be some benches and planted trees outside the building. Fill and use the whole building with the rooms/furniture.\r\n\r\nThe lobby/reception area should be the single largest room in the bottom floor. The cells should be smaller than the office rooms, you can make there be 3 or 4 of each as needed. Add some bars on the cell room windows. The stairs do not need their own room, they can be in the hallway connecting the rooms together.",
